WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.389
A bus carries information between components.

00:00:02.389 --> 00:00:10.752
An address identifies a location, data carries the value being transferred, and control signals describe actions such as read or write.

00:00:10.752 --> 00:00:15.530
Bus width and addressable unit together determine what an address can identify.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:21.156
Sixteen address bits represent 2^16 = 65,536 distinct addresses.

00:00:21.156 --> 00:00:28.866
If each address selects one byte, the address space is 65,536 bytes or 64 KiB.

00:00:28.866 --> 00:00:34.520
An eight-bit data bus does not reduce the number of addresses.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.498
A 16-bit byte address space contains how many addresses?

00:00:39.498 --> 00:00:42.150
There are 2^16 possible address patterns.
